# Group editor response publication correction

This work-only correction follows the source-bound negative review78 of the frozen group-editor candidate885. Neither old epoch nor installed production is changed. The full original885 and negative78 strict manifests are retained as exact reference snapshots; copied candidate code, tests, source-study17 and complete GPL license retain their original hashes except the four explicit client substitutions. It is GPL-2.0-or-later source-assisted code, with the existing original notices retained.

A successful Create or Save formerly checked group values after the active-entry list, then requested the final group list through a renderer that invalidated and replaced the form. Enabled name/notes changes during that second response were discarded. The correction fetches that final list before changing the panel generation, rechecks current view/form ownership and current values after it resolves, and updates the acknowledged UUID/revision while retaining newer values. An unchanged acknowledged form can then be rendered from the already-fetched list without another asynchronous publication boundary.

Group-generation, selection, bin invalidation, session/disposal and entry-effect restrictions remain. Name/notes strings, backend, persistence, KDBX/XML/history and original verification code are unchanged. Raw source MACs are still checked by the server. This correction does not add group settings, generalized moves, original GUI behavior, original-runtime imports, full KeePass parity, security equivalence or superiority.

The exact independent six-case negative/control bodies and five adjacent bodies are replayed with only four fixture import paths adapted. Their original9pass/2fail evidence remains immutable. New correction controls separately check acknowledged form clearing, late programmatic changes and subsequent singular writes using the new UUID/MAC, explicit panel closure, disposal, newer entry drafts and failed-write retry. DOM-model acceptance is distinct from actual browser acceptance.

Historical original22 managed loads (seven group-edit and fifteen group-recycle) remain evidence of the old885 epoch. No original is executed for this client-only correction. Root's historical real HTTP3/four starts and normal-browser8 campaigns are not rebound to these new client bytes. Root owns independent final review, actual current-browser validation and any eventual production installation.
